WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.430
- You've had so many great co-stars.

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:02.330
I love everything you're in.

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:04.430
So I hear you did own, though,

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:06.760
a life-size cut-out of
Sarah Michelle Gellar.

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:08.098
- Oh no, I still.

00:00:08.098 --> 00:00:09.836
- It's going in the coffin with me.

00:00:09.836 --> 00:00:12.105
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:00:12.105 --> 00:00:14.730
I'm into reduce, reuse, recycle,

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:18.340
and I go to estate sales like
a lot and it makes sense.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.430
I've gotten some good things
to Kelly Wearstler couch,

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.410
a Sarah-- a best friend cut out.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:24.200
And so I go to this estate sale.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.270
And while like Sarah's busy
living her movie star life

00:00:27.270 --> 00:00:30.280
in the Palisades. Working hard, kids.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.844
I am in Van Nuys

00:00:31.844 --> 00:00:33.360
(Kelly laughing)
collecting her

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.780
from someone that went away to college

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:36.530
in the 90's and 2000.

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:39.220
And I brought her home scared the--

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:40.840
and my nickname for her is "Scare-ah"

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.090
'cause I've always just called her that

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:44.760
cause she's so by the rules,
like, you know, "Do this!"

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.110
And so I'd always call her Scare-ah.

00:00:46.110 --> 00:00:47.300
Scare-ah Michelle Gellar.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:48.810
And now I have this cut-out.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:50.090
It lived in Arthur's room for awhile,

00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:52.360
but he'd fall asleep early
and I'd put it by the couch

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:53.990
so he'd wake up and she's right there.

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:56.052
I mean, it was really so many times a day,

00:00:56.052 --> 00:00:57.480
(scared gasp)
Sarah. But it's so good.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:58.970
- Here's where we're very similar.

00:00:58.970 --> 00:00:59.950
I had a cut-out.

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:02.320
It was given to me, both were given to me.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:03.940
One was Ellen. This was years ago.

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:06.330
And then one was, I think
it was Ellen who gave it,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:08.490
and then I got a Meryl Streep one,

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:10.150
cause I'm a huge Meryl Streep
fan, they gave it to me.

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:10.983
But here's the thing,
- Where did you have them?

00:01:10.983 --> 00:01:12.070
- I had it in my house.

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:13.690
Well, I had to get rid of them

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:15.836
because it scared the
(bleep) out of everyone.

00:01:15.836 --> 00:01:18.130
- Because they're just a
little bit bigger than people

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:20.770
where they look like a
goblin. Like it's dark--

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:21.690
- People would come to my
house and it's be dark.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:23.819
And it'd be like.

00:01:23.819 --> 00:01:24.680
Everyone would get scared.

00:01:24.680 --> 00:01:26.050
And my kids started getting scared

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:26.920
like a little bit at night,

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:28.890
'cause it's just like this big figure,

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:30.540
but I did have to get
rid of them eventually.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:32.550
But Ellen and Meryl Streep
- No, it's useful in COVID.

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:33.590
- Lived with me for a minute

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:35.260
- I would take those in a second,

00:01:35.260 --> 00:01:37.590
but Scare-ah is the best
and in COVID it was perfect.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:38.890
'Cause sometimes people would come in

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:40.120
and they wouldn't come in.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:42.750
She hasn't seen it in person,
but I'd bring the coat,

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:44.680
I'd bring it out and I'd
be like Amanda Kloots

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:46.070
like, "Okay, take a picture with Sarah!"

00:01:46.070 --> 00:01:47.190
And we would.
(Kelly and the audience laugh)

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:49.360
We'd have our masks on
taking pictures with Sarah.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:50.860
And she's now in my office.

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:53.586
And if I do zooms and I
know I have to stay on track

00:01:53.586 --> 00:01:55.040
- Please say you put her--
- 'cause I'm so distracted

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:58.177
- I do. She gives me
that knowing look, like.

00:01:58.177 --> 00:02:00.170
(Kelly and audience laugh)
And so I know not to say

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:02.170
things like, "Oh my god, I look so amazing

00:02:02.170 --> 00:02:03.210
after my breast implants."

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:04.795
Like just ridiculous stuff I said.

00:02:04.795 --> 00:02:05.628
(Kelly laughing and
scattered audience clapping)

00:02:05.628 --> 00:02:06.780
"Like you should've seen me before!"

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:07.663
And she's like.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:10.480
So I wish I had it right here

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:11.660
so I didn't say that
- I like the unfiltered.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:14.010
It's amazing, it's amazing.
- I am a jokester.

